            { id: "dsa5105-rl-q3", type: "short", prompt: String.raw`What happens to the weight $\gamma^k$ of a reward $k$ steps in the future as $\gamma$ becomes smaller?`, accepted: ["they are discounted more", "far future rewards matter less", "future rewards receive lower weight"], solution: String.raw`Far-future rewards receive less weight because $\gamma^k$ decreases for $k>0$, so the agent becomes more short-term oriented.`, explanation: String.raw`The immediate reward has exponent $0$ and weight $\gamma^0=1$; later rewards are discounted.`, sourceRefs: [reference("DSA5105/Ref/Reinforcement_Learning_an_Introduction.pdf", 1, "discounted return", "optional")] }
